t":"pub struct Adler32 {\n    a: u16,\n    b: u16,\n}","attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Adler-32 checksum calculator."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" An instance of this type is equivalent to an Adler-32 checksum: It can be created in the default"},{"DocComment":" state via [`new`] (or the provided `Default` impl), or from a precalculated checksum via"},{"DocComment":" [`from_checksum`], and the currently stored checksum can be fetched via [`checksum`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This type also implements `Hasher`, which makes it easy to calculate Adler-32 checksums of any"},{"DocComment":" type that implements or derives `Hash`. This also allows using Adler-32 in a `HashMap`, although"},{"DocComment":" that is not recommended (while every checksum is a hash function, they are not necessarily a"},{"DocComment":" good one)."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Basic, piecewise checksum calculation:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use adler2::Adler32;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut adler = Adler32::new();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" adler.write_slice(&[0, 1, 2]);"},{"DocComment":" adler.write_slice(&[3, 4, 5]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(adler.checksum(), 0x00290010);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Using `Hash` to process structures:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::hash::Hash;"},{"DocComment":" use adler2::Adler32;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" #[derive(Hash)]"},{"DocComment":" struct Data {"},{"DocComment":"     byte: u8,"},{"DocComment":"     word: u16,"},{"DocComment":"     big: u64,"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut adler = Adler32::new();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let data = Data { byte: 0x1F, word: 0xABCD, big: !0 };"},{"DocComment":" data.hash(&mut adler);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // hash value depends on archi